    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-05",
      "edition": "Thursday 5 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching backing",
          "heading": "RFU extends Steve Borthwick's contract to 2028, backing him through autumn results",
          "body": "Bill Sweeney, the RFU chief executive, has extended Steve Borthwick's contract by six months to mid-2028 and cannot envisage him being out of post for next year's World Cup in Australia, whatever the autumn results. The move comes despite England's worst Six Nations performance under Borthwick earlier this year, which Sweeney said he was very disappointed by. \"We believe in what he's doing,\" Sweeney said. He wants to see continued progress, and the RFU is backing Borthwick to deliver it."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland's Porter, Baird and Hansen return for Argentina clash",
          "body": "Argentina's Mallía returns from ruptured knee ligaments. Wallabies recall Kurtley Beale for northern tour."
        }
      ]
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-05",
      "edition": "Thursday 5 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Front-row cover",
          "heading": "Clermont sign All Blacks prop Ofa Tu'ungafasi for three months' injury cover",
          "body": "Clermont have signed All Blacks prop Ofa Tu'ungafasi on a three-month injury-cover deal, announced on Tuesday. The 34-year-old can play either prop position and played the last of his 68 Tests in November 2024. Clermont head coach Christophe Urios said: \"This is a fantastic opportunity that we've seized.\" Scrum anchor Régis Montagne will be away with France this month, and Clermont are missing Cristian Ojovan and Sacha Lotrian."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland's Porter, Baird and Hansen return for Argentina clash",
