    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-05",
      "edition": "Thursday 5 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad news",
          "heading": "Freddy Douglas and Ollie Blyth-Lafferty called up late for All Blacks test",
          "body": "Late additions Freddy Douglas and Ollie Blyth-Lafferty give Gregor Townsend more options before Saturday's test against the All Blacks, but the BBC's Tom English is more interested in who has been left out. English says Townsend clearly believes he already has enough carriers, calls Magnus Bradbury's omission harsh and suggests the coach does not trust him. Townsend had initially left Douglas out because of cover at seven, a call a reader asked English to revisit."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
