    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-05",
      "edition": "Thursday 5 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching verdict",
          "heading": "Ronan O'Gara says Wales' coaching ticket delivers progress; Japan win non-negotiable",
          "body": "Former Ireland fly-half and ITV pundit Ronan O'Gara believes Steve Tandy's coaching team is making progress, and that Wales should be judged on it. “Wins for Wales aren’t measured by victories now,” he said. Beating Japan this month is, in his view, non-negotiable. He argues that 14 of Tandy's 39-man squad playing in the Prem could rebuild the winning habit Wales have lacked at Test level."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland's Porter, Baird and Hansen return for Argentina clash",
