      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-05",
      "edition": "Thursday 5 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Contepomi makes twelve changes to Pumas side for Dublin, Mallía back",
          "body": "Only Boris Wenger, Guido Petti and Pablo Matera survive from the XV that drew 28-28 with Australia in September, for Friday's Nations Championship match at the Aviva Stadium. The headline return is fullback Juan Cruz Mallía, back for the first time in almost a year after ruptured knee ligaments from a late tackle by England's Tom Curry. Argentina have never beaten Ireland away from home in 11 meetings, and Contepomi calls Friday \"a massive, massive challenge\" one year out from the World Cup."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England's Borthwick handed contract extension despite Six Nations slump",
